      },
      "note": [
        "The statistics are classified as statistics under development and do not constitute official statistics. More information about the statistics and their quality is available in the quality declaration [on Statistics Sweden’s website](https://www.scb.se/he0110).",
        "The reporting refers to monthly income.",
        "The statistics are presented for two different populations:  \r\n- Persons registered in Sweden on the last day of the month preceding the reference month.  \r\n- Persons registered in Sweden on the last day of the month preceding the reference month with a value (income) different from zero in the relevant income category.",
        "Individual disposable income is the sum of a person’s taxable and non-taxable income minus taxes and other negative transfers during the reference month. Capital income is not included in disposable income in the monthly statistics.",
        "The following types of income are not available in administrative monthly registers. Monthly values have instead been estimated using models and subsequently included in the calculation of monthly disposable income. The model-based estimates for each type of income are associated with some uncertainty, which is carried forward in the derivation of disposable income.  \r\n- Self-employment income  \r\n- Taxable private pension  \r\n- Wage and pension income from other Nordic countries for persons registered in Sweden  \r\n- Child maintenance  \r\n- Occupational pension (missing 70 percent of total amount)"
      ],
